ting code","messageBody":"","tags":["A-Jar"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"md":{"insertions":6,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"418896aea9c013b5cd0c48b8cf665b6fb637529c","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add Javadoc header comments across codebase","messageBody":"Add class and method header comments to all non-private classes, methods,\nand test fixtures in both production and test packages to improve codebase\ndocumentation and maintainability.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":427,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"a82db560bc99dea975e934bd88e31f7afd350078","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027branch-A-JavaDoc\u0027","messageBody":"","tags":["A-JavaDoc"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]},{"date":"2026-09-01T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"90bc60c694346ffa7c1563ce9c76151296bd687a","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Refactor codebase to follow SE-EDU Java standard","messageBody":"Java source code contains stylistic inconsistencies such as exposed\nmutable fields in Task, non-standard boolean naming, redundant \u0027this\u0027\nqualifiers, unpunctuated Javadoc tags, and lines exceeding length limits.\n\nAdhering to the SE-EDU Java Coding Standard and Google Java Style Guide\nensures proper OOP encapsulation, readability, and long-term\nmaintainability across the codebase.\n\nLet\u0027s,\n* enforce field encapsulation and class element ordering in Task\n* rename boolean flags and methods to follow boolean naming rules\n  (isRunning, isDone, isTaskMatchingDate)\n* remove redundant \u0027this\u0027 keyword qualifiers across classes\n* wrap lines exceeding character limits with continuation indentation\n* standardize Javadoc tag punctuation and parameter naming\n* update JUnit test cases to match the refactored method names\n\nApplying predicate naming conventions and proper encapsulation prevents\nunwanted field mutation while keeping all observable behavior identical.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"java":{"insertions":179,"deletions":174}}},{"hash":"cb3fad7ab61d1ee290cace0568ca5d924a397427","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add SE-EDU Java coding standard skill and mandate","messageBody":"The project lacks an explicit skill and instruction mandating adherence\nto the SE-EDU Java Coding Standard for coding agents.\n\nCodifying SE-EDU Java conventions into a dedicated skill and referencing\nit in the agent rules ensures automated tools and developers follow\nconsistent naming, formatting, and OOP standards.\n\nLet\u0027s,\n* create the seedu-java-coding-standard skill in .agents/skills/\n* update AGENTS.md to mandate following the coding standard\n\nProviding explicit rules prevents code quality degradation during\nautomated refactoring and feature implementation.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"md":{"insertions":136,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"c78ddd9ccbffa5475025f48f1ba2d1a790cd1e3e","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add SE-EDU Git conventions skill and mandate","messageBody":"Git conventions for commit messages and branch naming in AGENTS.md are\nonly briefly summarized and lack a dedicated skill reference.\n\nProviding a comprehensive skill ensures all future Git commits and branch\nnames strictly adhere to the structured SE-EDU Git guidelines.\n\nLet\u0027s,\n* create the seedu-git-standard skill in .agents/skills/\n* update AGENTS.md to mandate adherence to seedu-git-standard\n\nHaving a structured template for commit messages ensures consistent,\ninformative version control history across all contributions.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"md":{"insertions":140,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"2f417e688f5e48321ae94d0ca03574f60b647ceb","isMergeCommit":true,"messageTitle":"Merge branch \u0027branch-A-CodingStandard\u0027","messageBody":"","tags":["A-CodingStandard"],"fileTypesAndContributionMap":{}}]}]},"authorFileTypeContributionMap":{"jamestorivor":{"java":2720,"md":999,"fxml":0,"sh":0,"bat":0,"gradle":2,"txt":0}},"authorContributionVariance":{"jamestorivor":213662.0},"authorDisplayNameMap":{"jamestorivor":"CS2103T-T17-3 TAN ..RCUS"}}
